   "title": "About this workflow",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Puts the face from a photo into a new picture (InstantID). The input picture is a clear photo of ONE face (front or 3/4 view).\nThe prompt describes everything else: clothes, place, style (\"comic art\", \"oil painting\", \"photo\").\nFace weight: 0.8 default; lower (0.6) = more freedom for style, higher = closer likeness.\nInstantID wants a low CFG (4–5). Avoid exactly 1024×1024 (adds a watermark-like pattern): default 896×1152.\nFace fix: the faces are found and redrawn sharper at the end (Impact Pack FaceDetailer; Fix faces denoise 0.3: lower keeps the face closer, 0 / bypass to skip).\n\nModel: SDXL checkpoints; Illustrious and Pony models work too (use their prompt style). Default: Juggernaut XL.\nDefaults: 30 steps, CFG 4.5, ddpm / karras."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
